in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @io
in @io/stagefreight
in @magic
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @io/stagefreight/narrative — the prose-projection species. The first
# concrete projection format under @io/stagefreight, rendering settled
# crystals into narrative text the receiver can read.
#
# Tick 67 of the refined /loop discipline; StageFreight cascade tick 2.
# Tick 66 landed @io/stagefreight family-root at b15c3f9; this species
# lands the FIRST forward-promised projection format.
#
# === The forward-promise this species discharges ===
#
# Per bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_out_substrate_ref.rs:23-24 (the existing
# RED test stub): `@io/stagefreight/narrative` is reserved as a
# projection format alongside @data/json, @data/yaml. This shard
# substrate-decl's that reservation — the namespace becomes
# substrate-decl ground rather than test-stub aspiration.
#
# Per the 2026-06-16 stage_play recognition cascade (Story → Play →
# Narrative): the crystal IS the play's settled artifact; the
# narrative IS the prose form ready for transmission. @io/stagefreight/
# narrative names the prose-projection at the wire surface.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# A settled crystal carries:
#  - oid (content-address)
#  - section (language-section structure)
#  - derived_predicates (verified-during-settlement properties)
#  - fracture_calendar (open opacities; the gold-cracks)
#  - composition_graph (DAG over @code/<lang> grammars)
#
# The narrative projection renders all five into structured prose: a
# story-form reading of the crystal that survives the wire and lets a
# human (or another agent) understand WHAT the crystal IS, WHAT it
# preserves, WHAT it left open. The narrative form IS the substrate-
# pull-correct prose serialization of the crystal's altitude
# structure.
#
# Splinter-pole narrative: prose-projection that round-trips structure
# (the receiver can reconstruct the crystal's typed fields from
# parsed prose). Narcissus-pole narrative: prose that reads well but
# loses crystal structure under projection (reader sees a story; the
# substrate-decl content is gone).
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `narrative_text` carrier: typed reference for the rendered
#   narrative form (prose; structured sections; readable +
#   reconstructable).
# - `narrative_projection` carrier: typed record (freight_manifest,
#   narrative_text, verdict). The substrate-architectural output of a
#   narrative-projection operation.
# - `project_to_narrative` action: the load-bearing FIRST consumer of
#   the family-root's `stagefreight_addressable` bilateral. Takes a
#   freight_manifest + perturbation; returns narrative_projection.
#   Requires the family-root's addressable verdict BEFORE projection
#   is admissible.
# - `narrative_grounded` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   narrative_text preserves the crystal's substrate-decl structure
#   under prose projection.
# - `finalize` action: substrate-vocabulary primitive for emitting
#   the projected narrative to wire_surface. Takes narrative_projection
#   + perturbation; returns wire_surface; requires narrative_grounded.
#
# === The narrative-survival discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 + the wire-survival discipline at family-root:
# when the narrative projects, the crystal's typed structure is
# preserved AS PROSE. The substrate-decl content is unchanged; the
# prose acquires sharper alignment with the crystal's structure than
# raw OID could carry. The narrative IS readable; the crystal IS
# reconstructable from the narrative.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   literate programming        Knuth 1984. Spec-as-canonical-prose;
#                               the substrate ancestor of prose-as-
#                               structure-preserving.
#   structured prose            McCarthy LISP S-expressions 1958.
#                               Prose that round-trips to typed
#                               structure. The substrate ancestor of
#                               narrative_text ↔ crystal.
#   reStructuredText / Markdown Goodger 2001; Gruber 2004. The
#                               cultural-practice ancestor of
#                               prose-with-structure.
#   stage_play recognition      2026-06-16 cascade (Story → Play →
#                               Narrative). The immediate substrate
#                               ancestor of the narrative form at
#                               StageFreight altitude.
#   crystal substrate-decl      task #268 (forward-promised). The
#                               typed input narrative projects from.
#
# === What this species does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT supersede other projection formats. @io/stagefreight/
#    json, /yaml, /brainfuck-compressed remain forward-promised
#    sibling species.
# 2. Does NOT prescribe a specific prose grammar. The narrative
#    section structure is forward-promised at species-extension
#    altitude.
# 3. Does NOT discharge the wire-survival of the crystal's OID; that
#    discharge lives at the family-root's stagefreight_addressable
#    bilateral. This species inherits the addressability check via
#    requires clause.
# 4. Does NOT depend on the crystal being fully substrate-decl'd
#    (task #268 pending). The freight_manifest carries crystal-as-OID;
#    the narrative projection takes the freight_manifest as input.
#
# Spec context: shards/io/stagefreight.mirror (the family-root;
#               declares stagefreight_addressable this species
#               first-consumes);
#               docs/specs/stagefreight-wire-v0.1.md (forward-
#               promised canonical spec);
#               bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_out_substrate_ref.rs:23-24
#               (the RED test stub awaiting GREEN per this species).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; narrative IS the prose-projection at
#                       the wire boundary),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: io/stagefreight.mirror (the family-root; the
#                  parent providing freight_manifest, wire_surface,
#                  stagefreight_addressable),
#                 io.mirror (the grandparent boundary family-root),
#                 mirror/store/crystal.mirror (forward-promised task
#                  #268; the crystal narrative projects).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/io/stagefreight/narrative.mirror` declares
# `@io/stagefreight/narrative` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/knuth-1984
source @arxiv/programming-languages/mccarthy-1958
source @arxiv/markup/goodger-2001
source @arxiv/markup/gruber-2004

prism @io/stagefreight/narrative {
  focus narrative
  project narrative
  split narrative
  shift narrative
  settle narrative
}

# === The narrative_text carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the rendered narrative form. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref. The
# substrate-output of the project_to_narrative action.
#
# Forward-promised refinement: typed record (title, sections,
# section_kinds, oid_anchor, derived_predicates_prose,
# fracture_calendar_prose, composition_graph_prose) at species-
# extension altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type narrative_text = ref

# === The narrative_projection carrier ===
#
# Typed record over (freight_manifest, narrative_text, verdict). The
# substrate-architectural record of a narrative-projection operation.
# Carries:
#
# - fm : the input freight_manifest (typed from @io/stagefreight)
# - nt : the output narrative_text the projection produced
# - v  : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → prose preserves crystal
#        structure; DEFENSIVE → projection requires substrate-pull
#        revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type narrative_projection = {
  fm: freight_manifest,
  nt: narrative_text,
  v:  verdict,
}

# === project_to_narrative action (FIRST consumer of stagefreight_addressable) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @io/stagefreight/narrative altitude. The
# substrate-vocabulary primitive for freight_manifest → narrative_text
# projection at the @io boundary. Realizes the prose-projection
# discipline as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a freight_manifest (the crystal under transit + its wire
# coordinate + its projection-format ref + the family-root verdict)
# and the perturbation under which projection is checked; returns a
# typed narrative_projection carrying the narrative_text and verdict.
#
# requires stagefreight_addressable(fm, p): the freight must be
# addressable at the wire surface BEFORE the narrative projection is
# admissible. This is the family-root first-consumer pattern: the
# species discharges the parent's bilateral before adding its own.
#
# Without this requires clause, a narrative projection would be
# admissible for a freight whose family-root wire-survival
# verification failed — the Narcissus-pole pattern at the projection
# altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
project_to_narrative(fm: freight_manifest, p: perturbation) -> narrative_projection
requires stagefreight_addressable(fm, p)
{ \ }

# === narrative_grounded predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# narrative-survival discipline. Consumer shards (finalize, below;
# forward-promised receiver-side reconstruction) name `requires
# narrative_grounded(np, p)` to declare bilateral agreement that the
# narrative_text preserves the crystal's substrate-decl structure
# under prose projection.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct prose-grounding check at the
# projection boundary. Composes with the family-root's
# stagefreight_addressable at the wire altitude.
#
# Bounded → prose preserves crystal structure (Splinter-pole);
# unbounded → prose reads well but loses substrate-decl content
# (Narcissus-pole; alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57
# distinguishes).
narrative_grounded(np: narrative_projection, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === finalize action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for emitting the projected
# narrative to wire_surface. Takes a narrative_projection +
# perturbation; returns the typed wire_surface where the narrative
# arrives.
#
# Per recognition #57: finalize operates at the @io boundary. The
# narrative_projection becomes a wire_surface preserved under
# narrative-grounding. The substrate's capability is unchanged; the
# prose's wire-survival is tightened.
#
# requires narrative_grounded(np, p): the substrate forecloses
# finalization from an ungrounded narrative. Narcissus-pole narratives
# (prose without crystal-structure preservation) cannot drive
# finalization. The bilateral predicate IS the boundary-harness at
# the projection altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual finalization
# is implemented by the @io transport (bytes-on-wire emission)
# consuming this bilateral.
finalize(np: narrative_projection, p: perturbation) -> wire_surface
requires narrative_grounded(np, p)
{ \ }

out @io/stagefreight/narrative
out narrative_text
out narrative_projection
out project_to_narrative
out narrative_grounded
out finalize
